{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And the reason for <b>and has not profaned it</b> is that the fourth year has not yet arrived, for the practice in a vineyard when its produce comes in is that flutes play there and people go about with them, and Scripture commanded (Leviticus 19:24) that all its fruit shall be holy, a festive celebration, that they praise the revered Name in that joy. And it is possible that the meaning of <b>and has not profaned it</b> is that he has not made it profane — and this is the redemption that our Rabbis mentioned (Mishnah Ma'aser Sheni 5:4) — from the language of 'for Judah has profaned the holiness of YHWH' (Malachi 2:11), and 'and he shall not profane his seed' (Leviticus 21:15)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "Flute-dancing at the vineyard harvest refers to the rabbinic description of the fourth-year produce celebration; Ramban links the root חל\"ל here to the 'profaning' that redemption from sanctified status effects."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:42.746144971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}